Created by PLY version 3.11 (http://www.dabeaz.com/ply)

Grammar

Rule 0     S' -> command
Rule 1     command -> action COORDINATE
Rule 2     command -> COMENZAR
Rule 3     action -> ATACAR
Rule 4     action -> DEFENDER
Rule 5     action -> ESCANEAR

Terminals, with rules where they appear

ATACAR               : 3
COMENZAR             : 2
COORDINATE           : 1
DEFENDER             : 4
ESCANEAR             : 5
error                : 

Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

action               : 1
command              : 0

Parsing method: LALR

state 0

    (0) S' -> . command
    (1) command -> . action COORDINATE
    (2) command -> . COMENZAR
    (3) action -> . ATACAR
    (4) action -> . DEFENDER
    (5) action -> . ESCANEAR

    COMENZAR        shift and go to state 3
    ATACAR          shift and go to state 4
    DEFENDER        shift and go to state 5
    ESCANEAR        shift and go to state 6

    command                        shift and go to state 1
    action                         shift and go to state 2

state 1

    (0) S' -> command .



state 2

    (1) command -> action . COORDINATE

    COORDINATE      shift and go to state 7


state 3

    (2) command -> COMENZAR .

    $end            reduce using rule 2 (command -> COMENZAR .)


state 4

    (3) action -> ATACAR .

    COORDINATE      reduce using rule 3 (action -> ATACAR .)


state 5

    (4) action -> DEFENDER .

    COORDINATE      reduce using rule 4 (action -> DEFENDER .)


state 6

    (5) action -> ESCANEAR .

    COORDINATE      reduce using rule 5 (action -> ESCANEAR .)


state 7

    (1) command -> action COORDINATE .

    $end            reduce using rule 1 (command -> action COORDINATE .)

